      "message": "fix(sim): sweep XY arcs exactly in the column engine, not as inscribed chords\n\nThe program sim's column engine cut each XY arc as chords drawn inside\nthe arc (chord_tol = cell/4). On a convex corner the arc's centre is the\npart's corner, so the chords brought the simulated tool up to one\nsagitta closer to the part than the real G2/G3. The issue's L-block\ncontour clipped one column 0.088 mm inside the riser's corner, and the\nheight verdict read that as a 10 mm gouge, so the post gate refused a\ncorrect program. On a concave corner the same chords stopped a sagitta\nshort of the wall and hid a real gouge.\n\nNew stock_sim::dexel_arc: disc, ball, cone and bull atoms swept along\nthe true circle. The per-column reach window is closed-form. The bottom\nis exact for discs and level arcs, and helical non-disc arcs are split\nat their curvature bends and searched by golden section (real\nevaluations only, so it never cuts past the tool). Arc end discs are\njudged too. XZ/YZ arcs keep their chords. The gouge verdict is\nunchanged.\n\nTests: the L-block repro over MCP (contour_arc_sim), an exact-reach and\ndense-scan check per atom, the issue's column, and planted convex and\nconcave gouges (arc_sweep). stock_sim's chord law is rewritten to the\nexact law. Bull column/field parity on the helix arc is bounded by the\nfield's own chord error, because the field engine still chords (follow-up).\n\nFixes #402\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
